[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:By Air]
[00:12.30]Why did the plane turn back?
[00:17.49]I used to travel by air a great deal when I was a boy.
[00:22.16]My parents used to live in South America and I used to fly there from Europe in the holidays.
[00:30.07]A flight attendant would take charge of me and I never had an unpleasant experience.
[00:36.65]I am used to travelling by air and only on one occasion have I ever felt frightened.
[00:44.07]After taking off, we were flying low over the city and slowly gaining height,
[00:51.06]when the plane suddenly turned round and flew back to the airport.
[00:56.51]While we were waiting to land, a flight attendant told us to keep calm
[01:01.80]and to get off the plane quietly as soon as it had touched down.
[01:07.30]Everybody on board was worried and we were curious to find out what had happened.
[01:14.08]Later we learnt that there was a very important person on board.
[01:19.96]The police had been told that a bomb had been planted on the plane.
[01:24.87]After we had landed, the plane was searched thoroughly.
[01:29.91]Fortunately, nothing was found and five hours later we were able to take off again.
